      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The current \"trending\" rip website is storing the vrchat ids for later download. They are infringing on the creator's IP by showing the avatar icon, however likely cannot be shut down with copyright infringement because they only present publicly available content. They also don't require much storage to support the website. They store any vrc avatar ids when they are seen, via mods.\nIf the website wanted to continue in the face of my proposed idea, they would need to download and store the avatars immediately upon seeing the avatar. This would require their \"users\" to upload the full assets and would require the website to pay for a lot of storage which would largely go unused when most avatars would not be pirated. They would also be subject to breaking numerous avatar creators licensing agreements. It would also make them vulnerable to attacks by uploading large amounts of large avatars which would go unused. All of these would present an uneconomical problem for the rip website and its creators.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
