      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{60344a7b306a6c0d3bc38dff|full_name}: manual approval would not be the approach I would recommend. It would be similar to safety settings, along with a manual share process if you click someone and say share avatar, kind of like the current \"show avatar\". All that being said, it could also be a toggle for the whole feature, some \"Limit Avatar Sharing\" option. Maybe they would have a eye with a cross in it by their name plate. Meaning they can't see your current avi\nAlso, the share settings may be saved on the server to avoid calling the avatar owner. There is no problem with that. But verifying the owner is in the same room would be nice. It would also be nice to let the owner know if someone loaded their avatar as a log setting. There is already a lot of data going back and forth, with all the positional and state data for each user in a room with you.",
